      <div type="clause" n="22.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 22.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>And ungetrywan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.7"/> men ceose man anfealdne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.8"/> að on þrim hundredum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.9"/>, ⁊ þryfealdne að, swa wide swa hit to ðære byrig hyre; oððon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/> ga to þam ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>An[d<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.3"/>] ungetreowan men ceose man anfealdne að [on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.4-2"/> þreo<hi rend="italic">m</hi> hundredan, ⁊ þreofealdne að], swa wíde swa hit to ðære byrig hyre; oððe gá to ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ungetrewe menn ceose man anfealdre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> að<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.4-4"/> on þrim hundrede<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.5-2"/>, ⁊ þryfealdne að<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.4-4"/>, swa wide swa hyt to þare byrig hyre; oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.6"/> to þam ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Incredibili eligatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.10"/> simplex láda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.4-3"/> in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.11"/> tribus hundretis, et triplex iuramentum tam late, sicut ad ipsam curiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.12"/> obeditur; uel eat ad ordalium.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="22.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Infideli autem homini eligatur iuramentum, quod Angli uocant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.10-3"/> anfealdne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.11-2"/> að, in hundredo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.12-2"/>, et triplex iuramentum, sicut conuenit curię illi ad quam pertinet; aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.13"/> uadat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.14"/> ad iudicium.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="22.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Infideli autem eligantur iuramenta hominum in tribus centenariis, et triplex iuramentum tam late quam ad illam urbem pertinet; aut eat ad Dei iudicium.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="22.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="184" ed="#robertson"/>And ungetreowan men ceose man anfealdne að on þreom hundredan ⁊ þreofealdne að<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IICn_22-1.robnote.fn.12"/> swa wíde swa hit to ðære byrig hyre, oððe gá to ordal<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IICn_22-1.robnote.fn.13"/>e.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="264" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ungetrywan men ceose man anfealdne að on þrim hundredum; and þryfealdne að, swa wide swa hit to ðære byrig hyre; oððon ga to þam ordale.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>Und einem unglaubwürdigen Manne erwähle man [das Gericht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.de.1"/>] einfachen Eid [durch] in drei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.de1.dagger"/> Hundertschaften [ansässige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.de.2"/> Helfer] und [wenn das Urtheil lautet auf] dreifachen Eid, [Helfer aus dem Gebiete,] so weit wie das zu dieser Gerichtsstadt gehört<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_22-1.lnote.de.3"/>; oder jener schreite zum Ordal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And for an untrustworthy man let [the court] choose the single oath [with helpers resident] in three hundreds [this and two neighbouring ones], and [if the judgment is for] the threefold oath, [helpers from the area] as far as belongs to that borough; or let him go to the ordeal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="185" ed="#robertson"/>And for an untrustworthy man compurgators for the simple oath shall be selected<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_22-1.robnote.n.1"/> within three hundreds, and for the triple oath, throughout the district under the jurisdiction of the borough-court; otherwise he shall go to the ordeal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="465" ed="#whitelock"/>And for an untrustworthy man one is to select a simple oath within three hundreds, and a three-fold oath from the area which belongs to the borough;<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_22-1.whinote.n.4"/> or he is to go to the ordeal.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="265" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And guarantors for the simple oath of the untrustworthy man shall be chosen from the three hundreds; and for the threefold oath, from throughout the jurisdiction of the borough court; otherwise he must undergo the ordeal. And a case requiring the simple oath of exculpation is to be initiated with a simple oath of accusation,</ab>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘anfealdre’ should be ‘-dne’; A should supply ‘ga’ before ‘to þam ordale’. In B, ‘on þreom hundredan ⁊ þreofealdne að’ was added in the 16th century in the margin.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 325, October 2026 (MS Cons); AV: corrected against Rabin p. 264, October 2026 (was “∅”, now “And a case requiring the simple oath of exculpation is to be initiated with a simple oath of accusation,”); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 264, October 2026 (was “∅”, now “| mid . . . lade: omitted A”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">to þam ordale: to ordale B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">mid . . . lade: omitted A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> sīplicia?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read sīplicia?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">attinet <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">attinet Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. geschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d written in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">on — að <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. am Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on — að in the margin in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">seligatur <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">seligatur K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in — sim. lada <hi rend="italic">überspringt HkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in — sim. lada skipped by HkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">curam <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">curam R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-triwe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-triwe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dre <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dre Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-de <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-de Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oþþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oþþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> -ldne</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read -ldne</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.4-4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ad <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ad A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> ga</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply ga</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.10-3" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dicunt <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dicunt Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-de <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-de Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.12-2" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur H;</hi> -de <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o on an erasure H; -de Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">gleichzeitig übergeschr. H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above contemporaneously H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später am Rande Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later in the margin Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Eideshelfer (nicht ‘Zeugen’; Leis Wl 14) werden hier dem Schwörer ernannt, und damit ist der Eid erschwert gegenüber 22; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Auswahleid 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The oath-helpers (not ‘witnesses’; Leis Wl 14) are here nominated for the swearer, and the oath is thereby made harder in comparison with 22; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Auswahleid 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.de1.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">[<hi rend="italic">dieser und zwei nachbarlichen</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">[<hi rend="italic">this and two neighbouring ones</hi>]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. I Atr 1, 3.⁴.⁵ = II Cn 30, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf</hi>. I Atr 1, 3.⁴.⁵ = II Cn 30, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_22-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bessere Übs.: ‘<hi rend="spaced">Gerichtsstätte</hi>’.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gericht 3a; Ordal 22</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Better translation: ‘<hi rend="italic">place of court</hi>’.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gericht 3a; Ordal 22</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_22-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">355</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘the simple oath shall be chosen.’ In this case the accused is not allowed to nominate his own compurgators.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_22-1.robnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>að</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">on þr. h…að</hi>. Added in margin of B in 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_22-1.robnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>ordale</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þam o.</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_22-1.whinote.n.4" n="4" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">465</biblScope></bibl><label>borough</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This means that he is not allowed to choose his own compurgators, but the court appoints them, according to whether the case demands a simple or three-fold oath.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
